# SPECIALIZED SECTION FORMATS

{% if ctx.section_title | lower | regex_search('anatomy|anatomical') %}
## Anatomical Section Requirements

For anatomy-focused sections, include:

### Layer Progression
Progress systematically through anatomical layers:
1. Surface (skin, landmarks)
2. Muscular/Fascial
3. Osseous (bone)
4. Vascular (arteries → veins)
5. Neural

### Measurement Standards
All measurements in: **Mean ± SD (range; n)**
- Example: "The optic nerve measures 4.2 ± 0.8 mm (3.0-6.5; n=45)"

### Anatomical Tables

| Structure | Origin | Course | Terminal | Clinical Significance |
|:----------|:-------|:-------|:---------|:----------------------|
| [Name] | [From] | [Path] | [To] | [Surgical relevance] |

### Variation Documentation

| Structure | Variation | Prevalence | n | Surgical Impact |
|:----------|:----------|:-----------|:--|:----------------|
| [Name] | [Variant] | [% (95% CI)] | [n] | [Implication] |

{% endif %}

